<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amalie Elisabeth of Hanau-Münzenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1602">1602</a>–<a href="/years/1651">1651</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Amalie Elisabeth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amalie Elisabeth of Hanau-Münzenberg was the wife of Landgrave William V of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> and regent for her son William VI from 1637 to 1650. During <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War she kept Hesse-Kassel in alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, held its army together and won the Hessian War against Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> she secured territorial gains and the recognition of the Reformed faith.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amalie-elisabeth-of-hanau-munzenberg.jpg" alt="Amalie Elisabeth of Hanau-Münzenberg" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gerard van Honthorst · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amalie_Elisabeth_von_Hanau-M%C3%BCnzenberg_(1602%E2%80%931651).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
